      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;http://wiki.rpath.com/wiki/Conary&#34;&gt;Conary&lt;/a&gt; has a powerful set of tools for package building that make packaging easy -- not just compiling, but maintaining, updating, and testing.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA; </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Michael will present http://wiki.rpath.com/wiki/Conary Conary] packaging, first demonstrating how simple the process is, then providing technical details of features that make packaging a simple, easy, repeatable process.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;He will show how Conary handles common cases automatically, while making it easy to override its defaults for unusual cases.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Michael will also demonstrate how Conary improves packaging quality, by making packaging consistent and by providing tools to analyze packages and collections of packages.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Last but not least, he will explain how Conary&amp;#39;s dependency management is different from legacy package management, encoding more thorough dependency&#xA;information without requiring cascading piles of irrelevant packages.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA; </description>
